msgid "Golden-furred Beauty"
msgstr ""

#. max 1999 bytes
msgctxt "1"
msgid "Caster's third SG.\nRather than a secret, it's a hidden identity/true nature.\n\nUnable to recall Caster's True Name, \nit's impossible to understand her foundation.\nHowever, it's clear that the encounter within that dream\nis something close to Caster's True Name.\nShe is a natural phenomenon that was deified,\na magnitude of energy different from usual Heroic Spirits.\nWhen tornadoes, tsunamis, or earthquakes are personified,\nthey are visualized as something that large.\n\nThe nine-tailed princess goddess was as ruthless and cruel\nas a god from ancient times, but at her foundation was\nplayfulness…… whimsy…… the same as Caster's.\nIn mythology, male gods emphasize rationality\nand female gods are concerned with sensitivity.\n\nOriginally, the fox was a Divine Spirit guarding the tomb\non the hill, actually the yin of the land's dragon veins.\nIn feng shui, only the yang dragon (energy for the living)\nis conspired with, and the fox with the yin dragon\n(feng shui energy for the dead) which was originally\nof equal or greater importance in the original feng shui.\nIt seems the origin of the form of a white fox\nrunning in a bright, moonlit night was also seen as\nthe afterimage of a single, long line (dragon's vein).\n\nSince olden times, trails of light made by the dawning sun\nover the sea or through the morning mist were associated\nwith snakes, dragons, foxes and the like.\nThe \"light of the sun reflected in water,\" in other words,\nan offshoot of the sun on the surface,\ncan be considered another of her essence\n(The Weight Stone of Tamamo is also a mirror stone\nreflecting sunlight from under river water)\nso, for this aspect, the most important is as a mirror,\nand then a circle as a motif of the sun.\n"
msgstr ""

